 "geometry_notes": [
  "Slab units and boxes: 'shear key recess detail' (BD-PC1): bottom 4 in band at the full width with a 3/4 in soffit chamfer; 3/4 x 3/4 in taper into a face recessed 3/4 in; 3/8 x 3/8 in taper out to a top 4 in band inset 3/8 in. The 3'-0\"/4'-0\" widths are at the bottom band. Interior unit (keys both faces).",
  "Box void: 5 in webs measured from the recessed face, 5 1/2 in top and bottom slabs, 3 x 3 in void chamfers.",
  "Slab voids: centred at mid-depth, diameters/spacing as drawn (36 in: 2 voids at +/-7 1/2 in; 48 in: 3 voids at 0, +/-14 in; S48x21: 12/10/12 in as labelled).",
  "PINNED: NYSDOT tabulated yb is exactly D/2 for every box and slab unit (not the true centroid, which is ~0.02-0.08 in lower because of the asymmetric key).",
  "PINNED: box Ix column is not smooth in depth (irregular second differences); residuals -0.4% to +0.9%. B36 areas match to 0.1 in2; B48 areas are 0.4-0.9% below the model (source area increments 28.9-31 in2 per 3 in, drawn webs give exactly 30).",
  "PINNED: S48x21 table (646.4 in2, 33426 in4) corresponds to three 12 in voids, whereas the drawing labels the middle void 10 in; the drawing is followed (+5.3% area).",
  "PINNED: S36x15 and S48x15 table areas exceed the drawn 8 in voids by 0.9 and 2.9 in2.",
  "PCEF: all dimensions drawn; the 3/4 in soffit chamfers are omitted (convention) because NYSDOT's table is reproduced exactly without them. PCEF-63 table Ix 500945 is a digit transposition of the computed 500495 (pinned).",
  "NEXT D/F: stems 5'-0\" apart, 15 in wide at the flange soffit (1'-3\"), side slope 0.375 in 12, R=4 in fillets, 3/4 in stem chamfers; D flange 9 in with the flange key-way; F flange 4 in with 1/4 in edge draft. Minimum flange thickness used (grinding allowance and fascia drip groove omitted). NEXT40D-120 yb read visually (27.37 in)."
 ],
